    <header>
        <h1>Entine Calculator</h1>
        <h2>Site Plan</h2>
    </header>

    <main>
        <section class="site-name">
            <h3>1. Site Name</h3>
            <p><strong>Site Name:</strong> Entine Calculator</p>
            <p><strong>Reason:</strong> This name represents a comprehensive toolkit for the fantasy world of Entine. "Calculator" suggests computation and tools, while "Entine" identifies the specific fantasy universe. The name encompasses all the site's functionality: character databases, magical creature information, translation tools, name generators, and interactive calculators. It's memorable, brandable, and accurately describes the site's purpose as a calculation and reference hub for fantasy world-building.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="site-purpose">
            <h3>2. Site Purpose</h3>
            <p>The Entine Name Generator serves multiple purposes:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Primary Purpose:</strong> Generate authentic fantasy names for characters, places, and creatures within the Entine universe</li>
                <li><strong>Secondary Purpose:</strong> Provide writers with culturally appropriate names based on different fantasy races (Randeth, Half-Elves, Demons, Dwarves, etc.)</li>
                <li><strong>Supporting Purpose:</strong> Integrate seamlessly with other Entine Calculator tools to create a comprehensive world-building resource</li>
                <li><strong>Educational Purpose:</strong> Help users understand naming conventions and cultural backgrounds of different fantasy races</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="scenarios">
            <h3>3. Target Audience Scenarios</h3>
            <div class="scenario">
                <h4>Scenario 1: The Fantasy Writer</h4>
                <p><strong>Question:</strong> "I'm writing a fantasy novel set in the Entine world and need authentic names for my Half-Elf characters. How can I quickly generate names that fit the cultural background and sound appropriate for this race?"</p>
                <p><strong>Context:</strong> A writer working on their fantasy story needs consistent, culturally-appropriate names that match the established Entine universe lore.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="scenario">
                <h4>Scenario 2: The RPG Game Master</h4>
                <p><strong>Question:</strong> "I'm running a tabletop RPG campaign in the Entine setting and need to quickly generate names for NPCs (Non-Player Characters) on the fly during gameplay. Can I get random names by race that sound authentic and don't break immersion?"</p>
                <p><strong>Context:</strong> A game master needs quick access to appropriate names during live gameplay without interrupting the flow of the story.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="color-schema">
            <h3>4. Color Schema</h3>
            <div class="color-palette">
                <div class="color-item">
                    <div class="color-swatch primary-gold"></div>
                    <div class="color-info">
                        <h4>Primary Gold (#FFD700)</h4>
                        <p><strong>Usage:</strong> Main headings, important text, borders, and accent elements. Represents the magical and mystical nature of the Entine world.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="color-item">
                    <div class="color-swatch secondary-orange"></div>
                    <div class="color-info">
                        <h4>Secondary Orange (#FFA500)</h4>
                        <p><strong>Usage:</strong> Hover states, secondary buttons, and highlighting. Provides warmth and complements the gold theme.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="color-item">
                    <div class="color-swatch background-dark"></div>
                    <div class="color-info">
                        <h4>Background Dark (rgba(36, 54, 39, 0.95))</h4>
                        <p><strong>Usage:</strong> Main background containers, card backgrounds. Creates the tavern atmosphere consistent with character pages.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="color-item">
                    <div class="color-swatch text-light"></div>
                    <div class="color-info">
                        <h4>Text Light (#FFFFFF)</h4>
                        <p><strong>Usage:</strong> Body text, descriptions, and content text for readability against dark backgrounds.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="typography">
            <h3>5. Typography</h3>
            <div class="font-example">
                <h4 class="font-heading">Primary Font: 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif</h4>
                <p class="font-description"><strong>Usage:</strong> This font family will be used for all text elements including headings, body text, and UI elements. Segoe UI provides excellent readability while maintaining a modern, clean appearance that complements the fantasy theme without being overly decorative.</p>
                <div class="font-samples">
                    <h1 class="sample-h1">Sample Heading 1 - Site Title</h1>
                    <h2 class="sample-h2">Sample Heading 2 - Section Title</h2>
                    <h3 class="sample-h3">Sample Heading 3 - Subsection</h3>
                    <p class="sample-body">Sample body text for descriptions and content. This demonstrates how the font will appear in paragraphs and general content areas throughout the site.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

